TASK 4 — CHOSEN STRATEGY JUSTIFICATION FOR CLIENTVAULT:
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RECOMMENDATION: Paragraph / Semantic Boundary Chunking ('paragraph_semantic')

Architectural Rationale for Client Support Runbooks:
1. Semantic Cohesion of Operational Steps:
   Client runbooks and SLAs (e.g. Acme Onboarding, Nexus SLA, Vertex DR) are
   structured as sequential procedural steps (Step 1 -> Step 2 -> Step 3.2 Dual Sign-Off).
   Fixed-size chunking arbitrarily slices sentences mid-word or separates prerequisite
   authorizations from action commands, corrupting grounding accuracy. Semantic chunking
   preserves complete steps and conditions together.

2. Perfect Section Traceability for Citations (PRD >=95% Requirement):
   Semantic chunking tracks Markdown headings (e.g. 'Section: Security Clearance & Roles')
   and maps chunks to logical runbook sections directly, providing exact [Source: Doc, Section: Sec, Page: P]
   citations without guessing boundary headers.

3. Optimal Balance of Precision & Token Economy:
   Averaging ~85-110 tokens per chunk fits within LLM context budgets while providing
   sufficient context for single-turn factual retrieval without paying for unneeded text.

